<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alauddin Riayat Shah II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1564</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin</a> Riayat Shah II was the first sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>, a son of the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>, Mahmud Shah. After the Portuguese took Malacca in 1511, he founded the Johor Sultanate on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor-river">Johor River</a> around 1528 and continued the struggle against Portugal. He was captured during an Acehnese attack in 1564 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a>.</p></div>
